Google Project Oxygen Case Study
This assignment regards the Google Project Oxygen: Do Managers Matter? case that can be purchased from the Harvard Business School website found in the syllabus. 

Submission Criteria
In roughly three pages please answer the following questions. Please only submit one case per team in Word format. 

How would you describe Google’s culture? How were managers viewed before Project Oxygen? 
What kinds of people work at Google? What should be the role of HR in such a setting? What should be the role of managers? 
What is your evaluation of the steps that the PiLab took to:
Identify the characteristics of effective managers at Google?
Roll out Project Oxygen to the organization?
Ensure that the Oxygen 8 attributes were widely adopted and practiced? 
What should Setty’s priorities be going forward? Which of the proposed initiatives should he pursue? In particular, should he and his team take on the challenge of trying to create “truly amazing managers?” If so, how? 
Evaluation Criteria
Case analysis reports will be evaluated using the following criteria: 

Content (50%). Does your analysis accurately reflect the principles discussed in the readings and in class? Do you correctly use organizational behavior terms and principles? 

Exposition (40%). Have you clearly articulated the justifications for your decisions and conclusions in the analysis? Have you indicated the assumptions that you made? Have you provided adequate explanation for why you made those assumptions? 

Presentation (10%). Is your report clearly written? Are your arguments easy to follow? Is your report well organized?

